evice \"Alice bedroom\" is offline') preserves the entire name in both message and stack. The secret-pair rule also stops at whitespace, so password=\"correct horse battery staple\" masks only \"correct\" and leaves the rest of the password. These paths violate FR-034 and observability-resilience OR6, which explicitly forbids device names and content in logs, even though the structured field allow-list rejects device_name. Restrict untrusted errors and causes to safe diagnostic fields or vetted bridge-written messages, remove arbitrary message content from stacks as well, and cover English names and quoted secrets containing delimiters in the redaction tests.","finding_id":"finding-73627a38ddb39b58","lineage_id":"lin-03d3cc7b6f865f74","location":"bridge/src/utilities/logging/serialize-error.ts:65","relevance":"current","resolution":"open","severity":"minor","source_local_id":"R1-error-log-content","title":"Untrusted error text bypasses the identifiers-only logging policy"}],"harness_id":"codex-cli-file-primary","run_id":"run-20261103-191955765-9ca7145b","runtime_outcome":"completed","schema_version":"1.0","started_at":"2026-11-03T19:21:38.8044050+00:00","summary":"Completed risk-based inspection of the frozen target's existing scaffold and utilities, including Entra sign-in, cryptography, logging, configuration, clocks, Pub/Sub, tests, CI and dependency gates, against the supplied design and contracts. One major logging privacy defect remains. The controller's single declared verification command succeeded for the supplied digest. No tests, builds or repository automation were run during review. This review covers the implemented checkpoint, not delivery of the application components still marked planned.","target_digest":"c79443ef9d0918d65613abc8c70057179467bf94","termination_verified":true,"validation":"valid","verdict":"findings"}